    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Japanese photographer and artist, born 1985 in Tokyo, educated at Tokyo Visual Arts College (graduated around 2007). Known for intimate snapshot photography documenting domestic and personal life; key series include Project Family (2007-ongoing), Still Life (2012-16), and Lovesody (2008). Gallery-represented by MISAKO & ROSEN (Tokyo), work held in SFMOMA collection, shown at International Center of Photography New York (2023), Maison Europeenne de la Photographie Paris (2022), Victoria & Albert Museum (2014). Nominated Prix Pictet 2014, Nissan Art Award finalist 2017. Senior independent artist level, roughly 15-18 years of active exhibition history; operates entirely outside any employer structure. Work Status: Freelance based on gallery-representation model with no employer, consistent across MISAKO & ROSEN artist page and blogspot portfolio site. LinkedIn not found; not expected for a fine-art practice. Autonomy 4: highly autonomous independent artist who sets his own projects and direction, gallery-represented internationally, but does not appear to direct others or run a team.",
